## 1. The desk in one picture

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    HF["Hedge-fund clients"] -- "bonds and stocks as collateral" --> DESK(("Financing desk"))
    DESK -- "cash loans (reverse repo)" --> HF
    DESK -- "total return on stocks (TRS)" --> HF
    HF -- "SOFR + spread" --> DESK
    DESK -- "re-pledges collateral (repo)" --> ST["Street lenders: money funds, tri-party, dealers"]
    ST -- "cash at the repo rate" --> DESK
    CO["Corporates, pensions, insurers"] -- "fixed vs. SOFR swaps (IRS)" --> DESK
    DESK -- "offsetting swaps" --> CCP["Clearing house"]
    TR["Bank treasury"] -. "balance-sheet, capital and liquidity budgets" .-> DESK
```

The desk sits in the middle of a **matched book**: it borrows cash cheaply against collateral in the street and lends it to clients a little more expensively; it takes equity risk from clients through TRS and offsets it by holding the stock; it takes rate risk from client swaps and offsets it at a clearing house. What is left is a **spread**, and that spread has to pay for the balance sheet the whole structure consumes.

