## 8. How the maths is validated

`pytest` runs the following checks (plus an optional QuantLib cross-check that runs in CI):

| Requirement | Test |
| :--- | :--- |
| Repo cash flows reconcile | purchase/repurchase price, accrued interest builds linearly to total interest, desk P&L = interest; collateral units and margin calls reconcile over the lifecycle |
| Zero-haircut behaviour | cash = collateral value, zero initial margin, any price fall is immediate exposure |
| Par swap NPV ~ 0 | 1Y-30Y swaps at the computed par rate price to < 1e-6 of notional and match the bootstrapped quotes |
| Fixed and floating legs reconcile independently | fixed leg = K x hand-built annuity; floating leg telescopes to N(DF(start) - DF(end)); every coupon equals the curve forward |
| IRS DV01 finite difference | central and one-sided bumps match the analytic derivative; error shrinks as O(h^2); key-rate DV01s sum to par DV01 |
| TRS MTM identity | closed-form inception value, mid-period value, dividend handling, delta; realised cash flows telescope and the hedged desk earns exactly spread - funding each period |
| Collateral and margin arithmetic | haircut / margin-ratio inverse, MTA, thresholds, rounding direction, close-out shortfall and recovery |
| Optimizer feasibility | the LP solution passes an independent limit checker; no random feasible allocation beats it; LP objective equals independently computed net income; frontier is monotone with falling shadow price |
| Rejected trade violates its reported constraint | every failure recomputed from scratch on the post-trade book |
| Netting cannot increase exposure | 2,000 random portfolios: net <= gross before and after collateral, gross independent of the netting flag, no offset without a netting agreement; netting-set EAD <= sum of standalone EADs |
| Curve | every quote re-prices exactly; flat quotes give flat par rates; parallel shifts exact; forwards compound consistently |
| QuantLib cross-check (optional) | discount factors from QuantLib's `OISRateHelper` bootstrap agree to 2e-6; 5Y swap fair rate and NPV agree with `OvernightIndexedSwap` |

## 9. Reproduce everything

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
```

```bash
python -m fsbs
```

That single command bootstraps the curve, prices the book, runs the optimizer, gate and stresses, writes `results/` (CSV and JSON) and `figures/`, and re-renders this README, [ANALYSIS.md](ANALYSIS.md), [MODEL_ASSUMPTIONS.md](MODEL_ASSUMPTIONS.md) and [RESUME_BULLETS.md](RESUME_BULLETS.md) from `docs/templates/`. Runs in about ten seconds. Tests:

```bash
python -m pytest
```

`make reproduce` does install, tests and the run in one step. CI runs lint, the tests (with QuantLib), the full pipeline, and checks that the committed headline numbers match a fresh run.

