## Glossary

| Term | Meaning |
| :--- | :--- |
| **bp** | basis point, 0.01% |
| **SOFR** | Secured Overnight Financing Rate, the USD overnight repo benchmark |
| **OIS** | overnight indexed swap: fixed vs compounded overnight rate; its quotes build the discount curve |
| **Discount factor** | value today of $1 paid at a future date |
| **Par rate** | the fixed rate that makes a swap worth zero today |
| **DV01** | change in value for a 1bp rise in rates |
| **Haircut** | how much less than the collateral's value is lent against it |
| **Initial / variation margin** | collateral posted up front / collateral moved daily as values change |
| **MTA** | minimum transfer amount: margin calls smaller than this are skipped |
| **Margin period of risk** | days between a default and finishing the close-out; collateral can move in that time |
| **Netting** | offsetting what you owe a counterparty against what it owes you under one legal agreement |
| **Leverage exposure** | the balance-sheet measure behind leverage-ratio capital rules |
| **RWA** | risk-weighted assets, the base for risk-based capital |
| **EAD / SA-CCR** | exposure at default / the standardised method regulators use to compute it for derivatives |
| **FTP** | funds transfer pricing: the internal rate treasury charges the desk for unsecured cash |
| **HQLA** | high-quality liquid assets held as a liquidity buffer |
| **CCP** | central counterparty (clearing house) |
| **Shadow price** | how much the optimum improves if a constraint is relaxed by one unit |

